  "body": "Hello everybody, I really hope this is the right place to ask this question, if not - please direct me to the right place and I'll close this issue.\r\n\r\nI've read [MDN's HTMLCanvasElement's specs](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/HTMLCanvasElement#Specifications), and saw that in Living Standard there's a method called `probablySupportsContext`. I also saw that this method is [being used by Modernizr](https://github.com/Modernizr/Modernizr/blob/5eea7e2a213edc9e83a47b6414d0250468d83471/feature-detects/webgl.js) to determinate WebGL support.\r\n\r\nHowever, when I tried to use it, I've found that none of the common browsers supports it, so my question is: Is it going to be supported someday? Is there like a page I can see the progress of those features? ",
